{
  "paper": "The Resurrection Connection to Christian Theology - Gary Habermas with @Real Seekers",
  "core_relation": {
    "sentence": "The resurrection is the linchpin that, if granted, entails a God who raised Jesus, the deity of Christ, the kingdom of God, and the truth of his teaching; all other doctrines hang on this one event.",
    "quote": "Now, if you put it together, this event happened. That requires this being. [S230-S232]"
  },
  "product_test": {
    "answer": "multiplicative",
    "quote": "If there's a resurrection, somebody had to do it... If Jesus is raised from the dead and his leading teaching is true. [S256, S262]",
    "reason": "Habermas treats the resurrection as a necessary condition: if it did not occur, the entire theological edifice (God, deity of Christ, kingdom, salvation) collapses. The relation is stated as conditional entailment, not additive weakening."
  },
  "slots": [
    {
      "slot": "G",
      "plays_role": "External negentropy influx is the resurrection itself as an act of God breaking into history from outside; coherence of doctrine cannot sustain itself without this external event.",
      "quote": "If God raised Jesus, if there's a resurrection and there's a God, you got to link the two. [S236]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "M",
      "plays_role": "Alignment is the correspondence between Jesus's claims/teaching and the resurrection event; the resurrection is the divine alignment with Jesus's own predictions.",
      "quote": "If Jesus is raised from the dead and his leading teaching is true. [S262]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "E",
      "plays_role": "Signal fidelity is the historical evidence and eyewitness testimony for the resurrection that survives skeptical noise; Habermas insists on evidential transmission.",
      "quote": "It's always empirical evidence like near-death experiences, uh Shroud of Turin, or historical evidence for the resurrection. [S108]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "S_eff",
      "plays_role": "Effective entropy is the skepticism, doubt, and competing miracle claims that lower coherence; Habermas treats these as noise to be answered, not as a factor that can be zeroed out.",
      "quote": "If they're really skeptical, no matter what I say will make no difference. [S084]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "T",
      "plays_role": "Temporal integration is the 15-year project and the cumulative historical case built across four volumes; time turns the possibility of resurrection into accumulated evidence.",
      "quote": "Obviously, this is a project that took you 15 years. [S023]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "K",
      "plays_role": "Compression is the compression of the entire theological system into two key words: theology and practice; the four volumes compress ordered meaning.",
      "quote": "The two key words in the title, what the resurrection means for theology and what the resurrection means um in practice. [S041]",
      "fit": "stretched"
    },
    {
      "slot": "R",
      "plays_role": "Phase transition is the resurrection as a one-time, unique event that changes state, not degree; it is a threshold that authenticates a religion.",
      "quote": "It's a one-time event where the evidence is very good. It occurred and it is for the purpose of evidencing a message. [S440-S441]",
      "fit": "direct"
    },
    {
      "slot": "Q",
      "plays_role": "Superposition is the open possibility of the resurrection before evidence is assessed; it remains unresolved until actualized by historical investigation.",
      "quote": "If something like that happened, yeah, it would be it would be the biggie. [S458]",
      "fit": "stretched"
    },
    {
      "slot": "F",
      "plays_role": "Non-local correlation is the connection between the resurrection and other doctrines (deity, kingdom, scripture) that are no longer independent once the event is granted.",
      "quote": "I think scriptures entailed somewhere down the line, just like I think ethics are entailed somewhere down the line. [S334]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    },
    {
      "slot": "C",
      "plays_role": "Integration is Habermas himself as the integrator, synthesizing evidence, theology, and practice into a unified case across 52 books.",
      "quote": "I've done 52 books and and by the way, I wouldn't know that except that I get asked once in a while. [S027]",
      "fit": "analogous"
    }
  ],
  "breaks": [
    "The paper treats the resurrection as a singular, unrepeatable event; the master equation is a general integral over all events, not a one-time threshold.",
    "Habermas explicitly denies that the relation is additive or probabilistic in the master-equation sense; he insists on a binary entailment (if resurrection, then God).",
    "The slot Q (superposition) is largely absent: Habermas does not treat the resurrection as an unresolved possibility but as a historical fact to be proven.",
    "The paper adds factors with no clear slot: the role of the Holy Spirit, the authority of scripture, and the personal commitment of the integrator (Habermas's own 52-year career)."
  ],
  "extra_factors": [
    "The Holy Spirit as an additional agent in verification and understanding.",
    "The authority of scripture as a self-authenticating source.",
    "The personal faith and commitment of the researcher as a condition for seeing the evidence."
  ],
